Subject: [PATCH 03/17] feat(refinery): gate mol-refinery-patrol merges on the
 approval signal (gcp-dc8)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wires the approval signal into the patrol formula behind an opt-in rig var, so
the refinery consumes what a reviewer produces instead of merging unreviewed.
require_merge_approval defaults to "false": rigs that do not require review
behave exactly as before, which is the whole reason the switch exists rather
than a hardcoded gate.

Turning it on implies the pull-request lane. merge_strategy=direct is promoted
to mr, because a reviewed merge needs a PR to review — without that promotion
the gate would refuse every direct-mode bead forever, fail-closed but
permanently deadlocked, which is the same dead end this bead is about. PR
publication then becomes the START of review rather than the terminal handoff:
the refinery records pr_url/pr_number first (the gate reads pr_number back to
confirm the reviewer approved THIS PR), runs the gate against the commit it is
about to land, and only then either merges via the direct path's existing
ff-only script or parks the bead. GitHub marks the PR merged once its head
commits are reachable from the base, so no separate PR-close call is needed.

A refused merge is deliberately not an escalation. Waiting on a reviewer is the
normal state of this lane, so the bead is left open and assigned to the
refinery with merge_approval_state=awaiting_review plus the refusal reason, the
optional review_agent is nudged, and the next patrol iteration re-checks. The
one place the formula does halt is a missing gate script while the opt-in is
on — an unreadable gate is not an approval. A rebase that moves the branch
changes the PR head and so invalidates a prior approval; that is intended,
since what would be merged is no longer what was read.

Note the rig-side half is not in this repo: gascity-packs turns the gate on by
adding require_merge_approval = "true" to [rigs.formula_vars] in the city's
city.toml, which is town config a PR cannot carry. The README documents the
exact snippet and the metadata contract.

Validation: test_refinery_patrol_consumes_the_gate asserts the wiring and
parses the TOML to pin the off-by-default guarantee (grepping around the var
block is not enough — the default sits after a multi-line description). Full
local gates green: gofumpt clean on the diff, go vet ./..., go build ./...,
go test -race ./..., golangci-lint 0 issues, validate_registry.py ok, and all
four gastown shell suites. Seven python pack tests fail identically on a clean
origin/integration worktree and are filed as gcp-cvb, not touched here.
